@.str.7 = private unnamed_addr constant [3168 x i8] c"\0A      Fetch a store path [closure](@docroot@/glossary.md#gloss-closure) from a binary cache, and return the store path as a string with context.\0A\0A      This function can be invoked in three ways, that we will discuss in order of preference.\0A\0A      **Fetch a content-addressed store path**\0A\0A      Example:\0A\0A      ```nix\0A      builtins.fetchClosure {\0A        fromStore = \22https://cache.nixos.org\22;\0A        fromPath = /nix/store/ldbhlwhh39wha58rm61bkiiwm6j7211j-git-2.33.1;\0A      }\0A      ```\0A\0A      This is the simplest invocation, and it does not require the user of the expression to configure [`trusted-public-keys`](@docroot@/command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-trusted-public-keys) to ensure their authenticity.\0A\0A      If your store path is [input addressed](@docroot@/glossary.md#gloss-input-addressed-store-object) instead of content addressed, consider the other two invocations.\0A\0A      **Fetch any store path and rewrite it to a fully content-addressed store path**\0A\0A      Example:\0A\0A      ```nix\0A      builtins.fetchClosure {\0A        fromStore = \22https://cache.nixos.org\22;\0A        fromPath = /nix/store/r2jd6ygnmirm2g803mksqqjm4y39yi6i-git-2.33.1;\0A        toPath = /nix/store/ldbhlwhh39wha58rm61bkiiwm6j7211j-git-2.33.1;\0A      }\0A      ```\0A\0A      This example fetches `/nix/store/r2jd...` from the specified binary cache,\0A      and rewrites it into the content-addressed store path\0A      `/nix/store/ldbh...`.\0A\0A      Like the previous example, no extra configuration or privileges are required.\0A\0A      To find out the correct value for `toPath` given a `fromPath`,\0A      use [`nix store make-content-addressed`](@docroot@/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-make-content-addressed.md):\0A\0A      ```console\0A      # nix store make-content-addressed --from https://cache.nixos.org /nix/store/r2jd6ygnmirm2g803mksqqjm4y39yi6i-git-2.33.1\0A      rewrote '/nix/store/r2jd6ygnmirm2g803mksqqjm4y39yi6i-git-2.33.1' to '/nix/store/ldbhlwhh39wha58rm61bkiiwm6j7211j-git-2.33.1'\0A      ```\0A\0A      Alternatively, set `toPath = \22\22` and find the correct `toPath` in the error message.\0A\0A      **Fetch an input-addressed store path as is**\0A\0A      Example:\0A\0A      ```nix\0A      builtins.fetchClosure {\0A        fromStore = \22https://cache.nixos.org\22;\0A        fromPath = /nix/store/r2jd6ygnmirm2g803mksqqjm4y39yi6i-git-2.33.1;\0A        inputAddressed = true;\0A      }\0A      ```\0A\0A      It is possible to fetch an [input-addressed store path](@docroot@/glossary.md#gloss-input-addressed-store-object) and return it as is.\0A      However, this is the least preferred way of invoking `fetchClosure`, because it requires that the input-addressed paths are trusted by the Nix configuration.\0A\0A      **`builtins.storePath`**\0A\0A      `fetchClosure` is similar to [`builtins.storePath`](#builtins-storePath) in that it allows you to use a previously built store path in a Nix expression.\0A      However, `fetchClosure` is more reproducible because it specifies a binary cache from which the path can be fetched.\0A      Also, using content-addressed store paths does not require users to configure [`trusted-public-keys`](@docroot@/command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-trusted-public-keys) to ensure their authenticity.\0A    \00", align 1
